## 4. Layout check for the longer name

"LUMBRA" is 6 letters; "SHADOW SKIRR" is 12 characters across two words, so the splash title must still fit.

- `.splash-title` uses `font-size:clamp(44px,min(15vw,22vh),170px)` with `line-height:.84`. `setLetters` already keeps each word `nowrap` and puts a breakable space between words, so on narrow screens it will stack as two lines (`SHADOW` / `SKIRR`) — that is the intended behaviour. Make sure it does:
  - not overflow horizontally at 320px, 375px, 390px and 430px wide (portrait) — if `SHADOW` overflows at 320px, lower the vw term (e.g. `min(13.5vw,22vh)`) rather than shrinking the desktop max;
  - fit on one line on landscape/desktop (≥ 900px wide) where space allows;
  - keep the per-letter `letterIn` stagger animation (second word starts 0.12s later — already handled by `wi * 0.12`).
- Header tag `shadow skirr · hiyroscript` is longer than before: confirm it doesn't collide with the `settings` chip at 320px. If it does, allow the tag to truncate with `text-overflow:ellipsis` rather than wrapping.
- Splash credit "a game by hiyroscript" stays as is.

